"Today's practice with Marta was a lovely little run — three attempts, three clear recalls, no hesitation needed. What stands out is how steady she was as the gap between check-ins grew: the jump from a quick first recall out to holding the answer for over 14 minutes, and then again to a full 16 minutes, without a slip. That kind of stretch without a miss suggests the interval was well-matched to her right now, giving her real, unforced success rather than a lucky guess.\n\nYou don't need to change anything about how you're running these sessions — this was a calm, confidence-building stretch. One small thing to carry forward: when she gets it right after a longer gap like that, a simple, unhurried acknowledgment (\"that's it, you've got it\") can help the moment land as a win for her without turning it into a test she feels she has to pass. Keep it light and quick, then move on.\n\nThere's nothing here that needs any adjustment or concern — just a good session to note and build on."
